  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Here en = ethylene diamine&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0144_20cc9f47f120.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 328px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;[PtCl<sub>2</sub>(en)<sub>2</sub>]<sup>2+</sup>&nbsp;forms cis and trans-isomers. Only the cis-isomers has no element of symmetry.&nbsp;So it is optically active. Trans&nbsp;- [PtCl<sub>2</sub>(en)<sub>2</sub>]<sup>2+</sup>&nbsp;form is optically inactive. Square planar complexes doesn&#39;t exhibit optical isomerism.</p>"
